Debian 13 "trixie" standard container template for s390x
=========================================================

Unofficial build of the Proxmox-390 project (https://proxmox-390.legitimatebusiness.be).
Not produced, endorsed or supported by Proxmox Server Solutions GmbH.

Same package set as debian-13-trixie-std-64, built for s390x. dab.conf differs
in Architecture, Version, Maintainer and Description; the Makefile excludes
s390-tools and sysconfig-hardware (pulled in by priority on s390x only, useless
in a container without CCW hardware). Without them the package list equals the
amd64 template's, minus dmidecode (not built for s390x).

Requirements
------------
- dab with s390x support: https://github.com/Proxmox-390/dab, branch
  s390x/arch-support (allows Architecture: s390x, adds the lib32 usr-merge link).
- An s390x host or VM running Debian 13 with lxc-pve (or lxc) installed: dab
  runs the target's binaries in an LXC container, so it cannot cross-build.
  Install lxc-pve before dab if you use Proxmox's lxc, and install xz-utils
  (trixie-updates/-security only publish .xz indexes).

Build
-----
  make            # -> debian-13-standard_13.7-3_s390x.tar.zst

dab writes its Source: lines into the template's
/etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian.sources, so keep the defaults (deb.debian.org,
security.debian.org) for a release build. To download through a local mirror
or proxy instead, add Mirror: lines to dab.conf, e.g.

  Mirror: http://deb.debian.org/debian => http://mirror.example.com/debian
  Mirror: http://security.debian.org => http://mirror.example.com/debian-security

Mirrors are only used for downloads and never end up in the template.

Published
---------
Built templates are published in the Proxmox-390 container template index,
https://proxmox-390-apt.legitimatebusiness.be/container-index/, which pveam
on Proxmox-390 nodes uses (signed with the Proxmox-390 archive key).
